    sheye sp <- find space...
```

Need to parse "a b". Find the space index. Write helper: find position of " " in line.

```
tosedo findspace(s)
    sho (sheye i <- 0; i < louwo(s); i <- i + 1) {
        wesosa (s[i] = " ") {
            cha i;
        }
    }
    cha -1;
bawoum tosedo
```

Then a = odresdra(substring before sp), b = odresdra(substring after). But no substring builtin! Need to build substrings char by char.

```
tosedo slice(s, i, j)   ' chars i..j-1
    sheye r <- "";
    sho (sheye k <- i; k < j; k <- k + 1) {
        r <- r + s[k];
    }
    cha r;
bawoum tosedo
```

Also negative numbers: e.g. "-7 2". odresdra handles "-7". Good.

```
sheye line <- diwela();
veshim (line <> malwe) {
    sheye sp <- findspace(line);
    sheye a <- odresdra(slice(line, 0, sp));
    sheye b <- odresdra(slice(line, sp + 1, louwo(line)));
    sheye q <- a / b;
    sheye r <- a - b * q;   ' careful precedence: a - (b*q) — right-to-left: a - b * q = a - (b*q). Actually correct!
    wami q + " " + r;
    line <- diwela();
}
```

Wait `a - b * q`: right-to-left: `a - (b * q)`. That's what we want. But to be safe write `a - (b * q)`.

Edge: what if line like "7  2" (two spaces)? Spec says separated by one space. Fine.

### t1-palindromes
Keep only letters and digits, ignore case. Printable ASCII. Need char classification. For each char c: letter if ("A"<=c and c<="Z") or ("a"<=c and c<="z"); digit if "0"<=c and c<="9". Lowercase: if uppercase, map to lowercase. Since ASCII, we can't do arithmetic on strings. But we can map via conditionals or use a lookup string. Simplest: build lowercased filtered string, then compare with reversed.

Helper to lowercase one char:

```
tosedo lowerc(c)
    moumare amdre c
    amdre "A"
        cha "a";
    ... 26 cases
```

That's verbose. Alternative: use a string "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz" and index: for uppercase letter at code, index = code - 65. But we can't get char code without... there's no char-code builtin. Hmm. We only have string indexing, louwo, concatenation, odresdra, ramou.

We could compare each char against specific letters. 26 cases in a moumare is fine but long. Alternatively, construct lowercasing by checking ranges then mapping with nested conditionals — still need mapping.

Option: moumare with all 52 letters mapping to lower. Write helper:

```
tosedo lowerc(c)
    sheye alpha <- "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz";
    sho (sheye i <- 0; i < 26; i <- i + 1) {
        wesosa ((c = alpha[i]) emsoulve (c = upper(alpha[i]))) ...
```

Need uppercase too. Two strings: lower and upper. For each i, if c = lower[i] or c = upper[i], return lower[i].

```
tosedo lowerc(c)
    sheye lo <- "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz";
    sheye up <- "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ";
    sho (sheye i <- 0; i < 26; i <- i + 1) {
        wesosa ((c = lo[i]) emsoulve (c = up[i])) {
            cha lo[i];
        }
    }
    cha c;
bawoum tosedo
```

Then:

```
sheye line <- diwela();
veshim (line <> malwe) {
    sheye f <- "";
    sho (sheye i <- 0; i < louwo(line); i <- i + 1) {
        sheye c <- line[i];
        wesosa (isalnum(c)) {
            f <- f + lowerc(c);
        }
    }
    ' compare f with reverse
    sheye ok <- shilsa;
    sho (sheye i <- 0; i < louwo(f); i <- i + 1) {
        wesosa (f[i] <> f[louwo(f) - 1 - i]) {
            ok <- ishe;
        }
    }
    wesosa (ok) {
        wami "yes";
    } oli {
        wami "no";
    }
    line <- diwela();
}
```

isalnum helper:

```
tosedo isalnum(c)
    sheye digits <- "0123456789";
    sho (sheye i <- 0; i < 10; i <- i + 1) {
        wesosa (c = digits[i]) {
            cha shilsa;
        }
    }
    cha (isletter(c));
bawoum tosedo

tosedo isletter(c)
    sheye lo <- "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz";
    sheye up <- "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ";
    sho (sheye i <- 0; i < 26; i <- i + 1) {
        wesosa ((c = lo[i]) emsoulve (c = up[i])) {
            cha shilsa;
        }
